{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Instead of bronze I will bring gold.</b> I will place in the hearts of the nations that they will bring gold. And the correct interpretation is: I will bring you a wage of gold. Now, bronze is more esteemed than iron; therefore gold corresponds to it in its place:" "<b>And I will appoint your overseers.</b> The men of your appointment, like פקיד, and they are the ones who distribute the tax:" "<b>Peace.</b> That they shall receive it in peace:" "<b>And your taskmasters [righteousness].</b> In righteousness:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:30.867570859Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}